IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja3-sch10-tenth-schedule.l4: the Tenth Schedule (cases where the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal can be exercised by fewer than 3 Judges).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone (SCJA1969.txt lines 6542-6584).  Answers seam 16 of PLAN.md; the asking section is s 60E(1), in scja2's range.
-- The Schedule allows a single Judge and nothing else, so the panel is JUST `a single Judge` for a listed matter and NOTHING for one not listed
-- (s 60E(1) says "if the Tenth Schedule so provides"); the yes/no twin answers JUST FALSE for an unlisted matter before the Court of Appeal.
-- Criminal: the Schedule is about the Court of Appeal's criminal jurisdiction, so the seat layer does not export it.

§ `Tenth Schedule: cases where the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal can be exercised by fewer than 3 Judges`

-- The matters the Schedule names.
DECLARE `sch 10 matter before the Court of Appeal` IS ONE OF
    `sch 10 an application under section 394H of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 for permission to apply to the Court of Appeal to review an earlier decision of the Court of Appeal`
    `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `sch 10 an order under section 378(5A) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal`
    `sch 10 an order under section 408A(4) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion`
    `sch 10 another matter`

-- The two consents the Schedule turns on.
DECLARE `sch 10 facts about the consents` HAS
    `each party consents to the relief or remedy sought in the motion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every party consents to the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Helper: one answer from several limbs.  Any limb that holds gives JUST TRUE; limbs that all fail give JUST FALSE; an unanswered limb leaves NOTHING.
GIVEN limbs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 the limbs taken together` MEANS
    IF elem (JUST TRUE) limbs
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF elem NOTHING limbs
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following cases may be heard and decided by the Court of Appeal consisting of a single Judge" [handed to a list, and no head in the list holds; delegated-definition ruling (a) of 2026-11-05]
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6554 | (a) an application under section 394H of the Criminal Procedure Code
-- src:6555 | 2010* for permission to apply to the Court of Appeal to review an
-- src:6556 | earlier decision of the Court of Appeal;
@ref Tenth Schedule para 1(a) (src:6554-6556)
GIVEN matter IS A `sch 10 matter before the Court of Appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1(a) the matter is an application for permission to apply to review an earlier decision` MEANS
    IF matter EQUALS `sch 10 an application under section 394H of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 for permission to apply to the Court of Appeal to review an earlier decision of the Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an application under section 394H of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 for permission to apply to the Court of Appeal to review an earlier decision of the Court of Appeal"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6565 | (b) a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal
-- src:6566 | Procedure Code 2010* for which each party consents to the relief or
-- src:6567 | remedy sought in the motion.
@ref Tenth Schedule para 1(b) (src:6565-6567)
GIVEN matter IS A `sch 10 matter before the Court of Appeal`
      facts IS A `sch 10 facts about the consents`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1(b) the matter is a criminal motion for which each party consents to the relief or remedy sought` MEANS
    IF matter EQUALS `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
       AND facts's `each party consents to the relief or remedy sought in the motion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 for which each party consents to the relief or remedy sought in the motion"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6574 | (a) an order under section 378(5A) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010*
-- src:6575 | summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal where every party
-- src:6576 | consents to the withdrawal of the appeal;
@ref Tenth Schedule para 2(a) (src:6574-6576)
GIVEN matter IS A `sch 10 matter before the Court of Appeal`
      facts IS A `sch 10 facts about the consents`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 2(a) the matter is an order summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal where every party consents` MEANS
    IF matter EQUALS `sch 10 an order under section 378(5A) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal`
       AND facts's `every party consents to the withdrawal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order under section 378(5A) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010* summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal where every party consents to the withdrawal of the appeal"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6578 | (b) an order under section 408A(4) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010*
-- src:6579 | summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion where
-- src:6580 | every party consents to the withdrawal of the motion.
@ref Tenth Schedule para 2(b) (src:6578-6580)
GIVEN matter IS A `sch 10 matter before the Court of Appeal`
      facts IS A `sch 10 facts about the consents`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 2(b) the matter is an order summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion where every party consents` MEANS
    IF matter EQUALS `sch 10 an order under section 408A(4) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion`
       AND facts's `every party consents to the withdrawal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order under section 408A(4) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010* summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion where every party consents to the withdrawal of the motion"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:6542 | TENTH SCHEDULE
-- src:6544 | Section 60E(1)
-- src:6546 | CASES WHERE CRIMINAL JURISDICTION OF
-- src:6547 | COURT OF APPEAL CAN BE EXERCISED BY
-- src:6549 | LESS THAN 3 JUDGES
-- src:6551 | 1. Despite section 50(1), the following cases may be heard and decided by the
-- src:6552 | Court of Appeal consisting of a single Judge:
@ref Tenth Schedule para 1 (opening words) and heading (src:6542-6552)
-- src:6571 | 2. Despite section 50(1), the following orders may be made by the Court of
-- src:6572 | Appeal consisting of a single Judge:
@ref Tenth Schedule para 2 (opening words) (src:6571-6572)
-- Seam 16 of PLAN.md.  The Schedule speaks of the Court of Appeal only, so for any other court the answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN court IS A Court
      matter IS A `sch 10 matter before the Court of Appeal`
      facts IS A `sch 10 facts about the consents`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Smaller panel`
`sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Court of Appeal` THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 10 the limbs taken together` (LIST
                  `sch 10 para 1(a) the matter is an application for permission to apply to review an earlier decision` matter
                , `sch 10 para 1(b) the matter is a criminal motion for which each party consents to the relief or remedy sought` matter facts
                , `sch 10 para 2(a) the matter is an order summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal where every party consents` matter facts
                , `sch 10 para 2(b) the matter is an order summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion where every party consents` matter facts)
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `a single Judge`
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule does not list the matter, and s 60E(1) allows a single Judge only "if the Tenth Schedule so provides"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule speaks of the Court of Appeal only
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:6542 | TENTH SCHEDULE
-- src:6544 | Section 60E(1)
-- src:6546 | CASES WHERE CRIMINAL JURISDICTION OF
-- src:6547 | COURT OF APPEAL CAN BE EXERCISED BY
-- src:6549 | LESS THAN 3 JUDGES
-- src:6551 | 1. Despite section 50(1), the following cases may be heard and decided by the
-- src:6552 | Court of Appeal consisting of a single Judge:
@ref Tenth Schedule (heading) (src:6542-6552)
-- The yes/no twin of seam 16 (assumed, not ruled: a result that is a panel cannot carry JUST FALSE).
-- JUST TRUE: the Schedule lets a single Judge hear the matter.  JUST FALSE: the Schedule does not list it, before the Court of Appeal.
GIVEN court IS A Court
      matter IS A `sch 10 matter before the Court of Appeal`
      facts IS A `sch 10 facts about the consents`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 the Tenth Schedule allows a single Judge` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Court of Appeal` THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` court matter facts
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Tenth Schedule so provides" [handed to a list, and no head in the list holds; delegated-definition ruling (a) of 2026-11-05]
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule speaks of the Court of Appeal only
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
